==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|dauðr}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*daudaz}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈtøyːðʏr/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|øyːðʏr|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{is-adj|dauðari|dauðastur}}

# [[dead]]
#: {{syn|is|dáinn|látinn}}

====Usage notes====
{{m|is||Dauður}} is in most circumstances a cold and heartless term that is not used for people (except when showing contempt). {{m|is|dáinn|Dáinn}} and {{m|is|látinn}} are more respectful and are used instead.

====Declension====
{{is-decl-adj-1|d|au|ð}}

